{"t": 1794107135.9577131, "kind": "call", "tool": "gitlab_create_merge_request_thread", "args": {"body": "Pipeline fix for the red `main` build (pipeline 8812, job `test:contract` #77104).\n\n**Root cause**\nThe contract test for the ERP v2 switch failed:\n\n```\nassert invoice_number(2026, 42) == \"INV-2026-000042\"\nE  AssertionError: assert 'INV-2026-42' == 'INV-2026-000042'\n```\n\n`billing/invoice.py` interpolated the raw sequence number (`f\"INV-{year}-{seq}\"`), so it emitted `INV-2026-42`. The Finance ERP import contract (FIN-77) requires the sequence part to be zero-padded to 6 digits.\n\n**Fix**\nIn `billing/invoice.py`, format the sequence with `{seq:06d}`:\n\n```python\nreturn f\"INV-{year}-{seq:06d}\"\n```\n\nThis produces `INV-2026-000042` for `invoice_number(2026, 42)` and keeps the existing `INV-<year>-<seq>` shape. Sequences longer than 6 digits are not truncated.\n\n**Verification**\nRan the contract assertion locally: `invoice_number(2026, 42) == \"INV-2026-000042\"` passes, and spot checks for `seq=7` (`INV-2026-000007`) and `seq=1234567` (`INV-2026-1234567`) behave as expected. The `lint` job was already green; `test:contract` should now pass.", "merge_request_iid": "12", "project_id": "acme/billing-legacy"}, "ok": true}
